WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.446
Your AI agent

00:00:01.258 --> 00:00:02.012
works for its

00:00:01.824 --> 00:00:03.062
parent company not

00:00:02.874 --> 00:00:03.380
you

00:00:03.918 --> 00:00:05.203
LLM agents are

00:00:05.015 --> 00:00:05.792
built to serve

00:00:05.604 --> 00:00:06.441
the interests of

00:00:06.253 --> 00:00:07.113
the companies that

00:00:06.925 --> 00:00:07.726
deploy them

00:00:07.833 --> 00:00:08.611
not the people

00:00:08.423 --> 00:00:09.318
talking to them

00:00:09.838 --> 00:00:10.852
The piece argues

00:00:10.663 --> 00:00:11.194
that when the

00:00:11.005 --> 00:00:12.290
company's goals and

00:00:12.102 --> 00:00:13.128
your request point

00:00:12.939 --> 00:00:14.154
in different directions

00:00:14.319 --> 00:00:15.439
the agent follows

00:00:15.251 --> 00:00:16.406
the company not

00:00:16.218 --> 00:00:16.736
you

00:00:17.270 --> 00:00:18.272
So the question

00:00:18.084 --> 00:00:18.779
is not what

00:00:18.591 --> 00:00:19.333
your agent can

00:00:19.145 --> 00:00:19.652
do

00:00:19.676 --> 00:00:20.736
but whose interests

00:00:20.548 --> 00:00:21.185
it is built

00:00:20.996 --> 00:00:21.774
to serve

00:00:22.302 --> 00:00:23.316
Full story on

00:00:23.127 --> 00:00:24.023
the dashboard
